# User Action States: hover, active, focus 🖱️

```css_not
/* 1. Mouse hover */
.btn:hover {
  background-color: #1d4ed8;
}

/* 2. Mouse click down (Active) */
.btn:active {
  transform: scale(0.98);
}

/* 3. Focus state (Keyboard navigation or click) */
.btn:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid #60a5fa;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

> ♿ **Accessibility Tip:** Never remove `:focus` outlines with `outline: none` unless you immediately provide a high-contrast `:focus-visible` replacement! Keyboard users rely on focus rings to navigate.

# Parent Focus: `:focus-within` 🎯

`:focus-within` styles a parent container if **any** child inside it currently holds focus:

```html_not
<div class="search-bar">
  <span class="icon">🔍</span>
  <input type="text" placeholder="Search courses...">
</div>
```

```css_not
/* Highlights the entire search container border when user types in the input! */
.search-bar:focus-within {
  border-color: #3b82f6;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2);
}
```

# Structural Selectors: `:first-child` & `:last-child` 🌳

Target items based on their position among siblings:

```css_not
/* First list item */
ul li:first-child {
  border-top-left-radius: 8px;
  border-top-right-radius: 8px;
}

/* Last list item */
ul li:last-child {
  border-bottom: none; /* Removes divider under last item */
}

/* Only child (applies only if there is exactly 1 sibling) */
.modal-btn:only-child {
  width: 100%;
}
```

# The Power of `:nth-child(an + b)` 🔢

`:nth-child()` accepts keywords, numbers, or algebraic formulas:

```css_not
/* Specific index */
li:nth-child(3) { color: red; } /* Targets exactly the 3rd item */

/* Keywords */
tr:nth-child(even) { background-color: #f8fafc; }
tr:nth-child(odd)  { background-color: #ffffff; }

/* Formulas (2n, 3n, 4n+1) */
li:nth-child(3n) { border-bottom: 2px solid blue; } /* Every 3rd item (3, 6, 9...) */
li:nth-child(n + 4) { opacity: 0.5; } /* Items starting from 4th onward */
```

# Form States: `:checked`, `:disabled`, `:valid` 📋

Style form elements dynamically as users interact:

```css_not
/* Checked checkbox or radio */
input[type="checkbox"]:checked + label {
  text-decoration: line-through;
  color: #94a3b8;
}

/* Disabled input */
input:disabled {
  background-color: #f1f5f9;
  cursor: not-allowed;
}

/* Live validation states */
input:valid {
  border-color: #10b981;
}

input:invalid:not(:placeholder-shown) {
  border-color: #ef4444; /* Only show red if user has typed something invalid */
}
```

# Pseudo-Elements: `::before` & `::after` 🪄

`::before` and `::after` insert cosmetic content into an element **without** touching the HTML markup!

```css_not
.quote::before {
  content: "“";
  font-size: 2rem;
  color: #3b82f6;
}

.quote::after {
  content: "”";
  font-size: 2rem;
  color: #3b82f6;
}
```

> ⚠️ **The Golden Rule:** A pseudo-element **will not render** unless the `content` property is defined! Even if you only want an empty colored box, write `content: "";`!

# Creative UI: Badges and Underline Effects 🎨

Create animated hover underlines with `::after`:

```html_not
<a href="#" class="animated-link">Explore Courses</a>
```

```css_not
.animated-link {
  position: relative;
  text-decoration: none;
  color: #0f172a;
}

.animated-link::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  bottom: -2px;
  left: 0;
  width: 0; /* Starts at 0 width */
  height: 2px;
  background-color: #2563eb;
  transition: width 0.3s ease;
}

.animated-link:hover::after {
  width: 100%; /* Expands across on hover! */
}
```

# Typographic Elements: `::first-letter` & `::selection` 📰

## 1. Magazine Drop Caps (`::first-letter`):
```css_not
p.article-intro::first-letter {
  font-size: 3.5rem;
  float: left;
  line-height: 1;
  margin-right: 8px;
  color: #1e293b;
  font-family: serif;
}
```

## 2. Custom Text Highlight Color (`::selection`):
```css_not
::selection {
  background-color: #fef08a; /* Yellow highlight */
  color: #0f172a;
}
```

# The Negation Pseudo-Class: `:not()` 🚫

Selects elements that do **not** match a selector:

```css_not
/* Adds bottom border to all list items EXCEPT the last one! */
li:not(:last-child) {
  border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
}

/* Style all buttons except disabled ones */
button:not(:disabled):hover {
  cursor: pointer;
  background-color: #2563eb;
}
```

# Modern Grouping: `:is()` and `:where()` 🧩

Simplifies repetitive nested selectors:

```css_not
/* Old Repetitive Way */
header h1, header h2, header h3,
nav h1, nav h2, nav h3 {
  color: #1e293b;
}

/* Modern :is() Way */
:is(header, nav) :is(h1, h2, h3) {
  color: #1e293b;
}
```

## `:is()` vs `:where()`:
- `:is()` takes the specificity of its most specific argument.
- `:where()` **always has 0 specificity**! Great for design system resets that are effortless to override.

# The Holy Grail: The `:has()` Parent Selector 🏆

For 25 years, developers begged for a CSS "parent selector". In modern CSS, `:has()` makes it possible!

```css_not
/* Style a card if it contains a featured badge inside it! */
.card:has(.featured-badge) {
  border: 2px solid #f59e0b;
  background-color: #fffbeb;
}

/* Style form label when its input is invalid */
label:has(+ input:invalid) {
  color: red;
}
```

`:has()` checks if a parent contains elements matching a selector!

# Customizing `::marker` and `::placeholder` 🎯

```css_not
/* Custom input placeholder text styling */
input::placeholder {
  color: #94a3b8;
  font-style: italic;
}

/* Custom list item marker */
li::marker {
  color: #3b82f6;
  font-size: 1.2em;
}
```

# Chaining Multiple Pseudo-Classes ⛓️

You can chain multiple pseudo-classes together for pinpoint targeting:

```css_not
/* An input that is required, currently invalid, and has user focus */
input:required:invalid:focus {
  border-color: #ef4444;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.2);
}

/* The first button that is not disabled */
button:not(:disabled):first-of-type {
  font-weight: 700;
}
```

# Real-World: Notification Banner with ::before 🔔

```html_not
<div class="alert alert-info">
  <p>Your subscription renewal is scheduled for next Monday.</p>
</div>
```

```css_not
.alert {
  position: relative;
  padding: 16px 20px 16px 48px;
  border-radius: 8px;
  background-color: #eff6ff;
  color: #1e3a8a;
  border: 1px solid #bfdbfe;
}

.alert-info::before {
  content: "ℹ️";
  position: absolute;
  top: 16px;
  left: 16px;
  font-size: 1.25rem;
}
```
